# Keep the working tree on LF, whatever platform it was checked out on.
#
# The stored expected output needs it because Hugo copies template text into
# its output verbatim, so on a CRLF checkout the generated HTML is CRLF too.
# Storing those bytes as-is would make a baseline depend on which platform
# generated it, and regenerating on the other one would rewrite every file as
# pure line-ending churn.
#
# The fixtures need it for a sharper reason. A site below tests/sites feeds the
# theme's asset busting, which hashes a file as it lies in the working tree, so
# a CRLF checkout and an LF checkout give the same fixture asset two different
# published names - and a name is not something the runner can normalise the
# way it normalises the line endings inside a file.
#
# Git detects the fonts and images as binary on its own and leaves them alone.
* text=auto eol=lf
